# LINE ENDINGS ARE LF IN THE REPOSITORY, whatever the working tree uses.
#
# Why this file exists: the maintainer's Windows checkout has
# core.autocrlf=true, so files land in the tree with CRLF; an agent
# working through a mount writes LF. Without a rule the two disagree and
# every touched file reads as entirely rewritten -- one checkpoint commit
# showed 24,900 insertions across 51 files when five files had actually
# changed, and `git blame` on the other 46 now points at that commit
# rather than at whoever wrote the line. Normalising once, here, stops it
# recurring and is why the renormalise commit beside this file exists.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
